# Docker-in-Docker runner operates privileged mode on Talos Linux nodes to manage containerized sandboxes
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0017 (Privileged)
KSV-0017
AVD-KSV-0017

# Docker daemon runner and API service require writable runtime paths (/var/lib/docker, /tmp) on root filesystem
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014 (Root file system is not read-only)
KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0014

# Upstream n8n-sandbox-service chart manages container-level securityContext internally without exposing drop-all or non-root overrides
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0118 (Default security context configured)
KSV-0118
AVD-KSV-0118

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001 (Can elevate its own privileges)
KSV-0001
AVD-KSV-0001

# Docker daemon inside DinD runner container runs as root to initialize container isolation namespaces and cgroups
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012 (Runs as root user)
KSV-0012
AVD-KSV-0012

# DinD runner requires unconfined / default seccomp profiles for container execution
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0104 (Seccomp policies disabled)
KSV-0104
AVD-KSV-0104

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0030 (Runtime/Default Seccomp profile not set)
KSV-0030
AVD-KSV-0030

# DinD runner requires kernel capabilities for cgroup and container orchestration beyond NET_BIND_SERVICE
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all)
KSV-0003
AVD-KSV-0003

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any)
KSV-0004
AVD-KSV-0004

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0106 (Container capabilities must only include NET_BIND_SERVICE)
KSV-0106
AVD-KSV-0106

# False positive: sandbox configmaps contain configuration keys (e.g. idle timeout, listen addresses), actual API secrets reside in n8n-sandbox-auth Secret
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-01010 (ConfigMap with sensitive content)
KSV-01010
AVD-KSV-01010
